 ],
 "literal": "Slender hanging roots of the fig tree climbing on the rock / like a waterfall descending from the mountain appear, the man of such a land / faultless heart's words towards us / has come, may you live, friend! We also / like fire with poured ghee, welcoming / 'we are as if married by him' let us send a messenger!",
 "translation": "O friend, may you live long! A message from the faultless heart of the lord of the land—where the slender aerial roots of the rock-climbing fig tree look like a waterfall cascading down the mountain—has reached us. Let us also receive it like a fire fed with ghee, and send a messenger back to him, saying, 'We are as good as wedded to you.'",
 "modern": "தோழியே, நீ வாழ்க! பாறையில் படர்ந்து வளரும் இற்றி மரத்தின் மெல்லிய விழுதுகள், மலையிலிருந்து இறங்கும் அருவியைப் போலத் தோன்றும் நாட்டின் தலைவனுடைய குற்றமில்லாத நெஞ்சத்திலிருந்து வந்த வார்த்தைகள் நம்மை வந்தடைந்துள்ளன. நாமும் நெய் ஊற்றப்பட்ட நெருப்பைப் போல அதனை எதிர்கொண்டு ஏற்றுக்கொண்டு, 'அவன் நம்மை மணந்து கொண்டது போன்ற மகிழ்ச்சியில் இருக்கிறோம்' என்று கூறி அவனிடம் தூது அனுப்புவோம்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend upon receiving a reassuring message of love from the hero. She describes the hero's mountainous land where the white roots of the rock-climbing fig tree hang down, resembling a beautiful waterfall. This imagery of the Kuriñci landscape reflects the strength and enduring nature of the hero's love. The heroine compares her joyful acceptance of his words to a fire that blazes up when ghee is poured into it. Overjoyed by his commitment, she eagerly suggests sending a messenger back to him to convey that they already feel united in marriage.",
